d/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-75829"] :question/problem "The following table gives the values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(3).$\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-9$ | $0$ |\n| $5$ | $3$ | $-2$ |" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=3,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(3)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(3)=5$ and ${f}^{′}(5)=-2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(3) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["q-75829/selection/ma-v1/6628defb4eae99b60781c2aa15cc0bf200f23848d6d435b1d0093d1b2f7a4fce"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-76114"] :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+2x+1.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(1).$" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(1),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(1)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(1))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(1).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(1)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(1) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =1 \\\\ {x}^{3}+2x+1 & =1 \\\\ x({x}^{2}+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(1)=0.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{3}+2x+1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =3{x}^{2}+2 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =3\\cdot 0+2 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(1))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-110338/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "2aedf132-d24d-5212-9f42-ff8047e1aa2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110338/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "c556d14b-70e2-5ca2-a713-25a69f146954" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110338/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "e2d66724-67af-5fbb-b742-1db1094234b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110338/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "7e593f1f-62bc-5168-932e-59309def1365" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110338/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "45bd1e36-3565-5059-9978-17a29caaedef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110338/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a6d83d3-c1bc-5852-905d-98bc3e78e569" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110338/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-110338/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-110338/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-110338/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-110338/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" "q-110338/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110338" :question/id #uuid "c30c5f22-36f0-5965-9fed-d4b105565e9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-110338" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac{x+10}{x+1}.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4).$" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(4),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(4)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(4).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(4)=x.$ For $x\\ne -1,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(4) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =4 \\\\ \\frac{x+10}{x+1} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{x+10}{x+1}\\cdot (x+1) & =4\\cdot (x+1) \\\\ \\frac{x+10}{\\cancel{(x+1)}}\\cdot \\cancel{(x+1)} & =4x+4 \\\\ x+10 & =4x+4 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(4)=2.$\n\nNow we calculate ${f}^{′}(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+10}{x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{9}{(x+1)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =-\\frac{9}{{(2+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{{(3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{9} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(4))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-110338/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b2a80aa-7882-50eb-bfe0-c0eeab72161d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110338"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-312585/field-1/393522ee4ded7288062e6072c329c38ecb06c9de712f11faf938346737b8d6d5" :answer/id #uuid "c1f55afc-34aa-53e1-8394-f61ac6801b80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-312585/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b00cba8-1263-5ce0-b5e1-148424743a6a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-312585/field-1/393522ee4ded7288062e6072c329c38ecb06c9de712f11faf938346737b8d6d5" :answer-field/choices ["q-312585/field-1/393522ee4ded7288062e6072c329c38ecb06c9de712f11faf938346737b8d6d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-312585" :question/id #uuid "7cdbca75-994b-53ca-b31e-22e3ae38d84f" :question/math-academy-id "q-312585" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-2{x}^{2}.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain $x\\ge 1,$ determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(8).$\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(8)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(8),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(8)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(8))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(8).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(8)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(8) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =8 \\\\ {x}^{4}-2{x}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{4}-2{x}^{2}-8 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4)({x}^{2}+2) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of $y=f(x)$ is $x\\ge 1,$ we have ${f}^{-1}(8)=2.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{4}-2{x}^{2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3}-4x \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =4({2}^{3})-4(2) \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(8) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(8))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-312585/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b2a80aa-7882-50eb-bfe0-c0eeab72161d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-312585"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342599/field-1/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "0f224817-f1c2-52b8-a838-c6627808bcbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342599/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "571a121e-249d-519e-92f9-1f1502bde7c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342599/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "03616ae6-f9da-5572-920b-0d866b07f62d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342599/field-1/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer-field/choices ["q-342599/field-1/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" "q-342599/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342599" :question/id #uuid "08e8f5ed-5b1e-519e-b4c4-4b136ca13f18" :question/math-academy-id "q-342599" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{2}-x.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain $x\\le -1,$ determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2).$\n\n$({f}^{-1})^{′}(2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(2),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(2).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(2)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(2) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =2 \\\\ {x}^{2}-x & =2 \\\\ {x}^{2}-x-2 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x-2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the domain of $y=f(x)$ is $x\\le -1,$ we have ${f}^{-1}(2)=-1.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(-1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{2}-x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =2x-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =2(-1)-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(2))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-3)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342599/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b2a80aa-7882-50eb-bfe0-c0eeab72161d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342599"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76128/selection/0f9ff88f8a509dc086c6b2ed1cead4f361d801dda530de5aba630613695847d5" :answer/id #uuid "59821fc8-e9df-5397-8f51-eb936149f62d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{e}^{-4}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76128/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "a3d66dab-93a0-5e57-b08d-c5fef1224017" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76128/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "f1e7b9cc-271b-5641-9a48-5cb756f4d2e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76128/selection/b941fa6c8f2aa2d152fa7f1a25f10235e524ca50f51af81ce5a50c5a9fc7e9da" :answer/id #uuid "35a03d42-f1c5-5c7f-ba9d-b0db949ac390" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76128/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "3bea40ac-6a9a-5644-8b15-d06af405881c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76128/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "521de4c2-d1f7-5a30-9d43-b3d0a36305f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76128/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-76128/selection/0f9ff88f8a509dc086c6b2ed1cead4f361d801dda530de5aba630613695847d5" "q-76128/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-76128/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-76128/selection/b941fa6c8f2aa2d152fa7f1a25f10235e524ca50f51af81ce5a50c5a9fc7e9da" "q-76128/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76128" :question/id #uuid "8be70d73-596d-5442-ba07-c1e2659c3b4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-76128" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=1+2{e}^{x+1}.$ Given that $y=f(x)$ is invertible throughout its domain, determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(3).$" :question/worked-solution "To determine $({f}^{-1})^{′}(3),$ we use the following formula:\n\n$$\n{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(3)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the value of ${f}^{-1}(3).$ To do this, we solve the equation ${f}^{-1}(3)=x.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{-1}(3) & =x \\\\ f(x) & =3 \\\\ 1+2{e}^{x+1} & =3 \\\\ 2{e}^{x+1} & =2 \\\\ {e}^{x+1} & =1 \\\\ x+1 & =0 \\\\ x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${f}^{-1}(3)=-1.$\n\nNow, we calculate ${f}^{′}(-1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =1+2{e}^{x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =2{e}^{x+1} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =2{e}^{0} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({f}^{-1})}^{′}(3) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(3))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76128/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b2a80aa-7882-50eb-bfe0-c0eeab72161d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76128"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-14720"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037063/assets/8fb287885c948b7e563b5fa878dd204dacbedea311490c4573aa883bff992662.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of a function $y=f(x)$ and its inverse $y=f^{-1}(x).$ The point $A$ has coordinates $(2, 0)$ and lies on $y=f(x).$\nThe point $B$ has coordinates $(0,2)$ and lies on $y=f^{-1}(x).$ If $f'(2)=-\\dfrac{3}{2},$ what is $(f^{-1})'(0)?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
